.TH "LEAN" "1" "Oct 2026" "lean" "lean Manual"

.SH NAME
lean-config - View and manage Lean configuration

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlean config [flags]\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
Project configuration is stored in .lean/lean.toml. User-wide configuration is stored in ~/.lean/config.toml.

Local configuration contains project settings such as the default profile, schema path, and output format. Global configuration contains user settings such as the editor and secret backend.

.SH EXAMPLES
  lean config
  lean config init
  lean config init --global
  lean config edit
  lean config edit --global
  lean config set --default-profile development
  lean config set --global --editor nvim
  lean config set --global --secrets-backend age

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlean(1)\fP, \fBlean-config-init(1)\fP, \fBlean-config-set(1)\fP

